"""Opt-in area-centroid placement of an ordinary direct-quad core hub.

The existing Coons blocks are affine in their common hub. Change only that
hub contribution; preserve every corner-band/guide vertex, face and attribute.
The candidate uses a fixed extrapolation of the core polygon's area centroid
from the current hub. It is a cheap continuous heuristic, not a shape proof.
The complete caller must retain all cell, overlap, boundary and height guards.
This builder is experimental and is not installed in any public recipe.
"""
import bpy
from . import curved_multisided_quad_nodes as cyclic

